{
    "background_story": "Aidan was a renowned entomologist who spent his career studying the unique properties of the derris plant. Native to the tropical regions of Asia, the derris plant had long been used by indigenous communities as a natural insecticide. Aidan's fascination with the plant's potential led him to dedicate his research to understanding its chemical composition and applications. His breakthrough discovery of the plant's active compound, rotenone, revolutionized the field of pest control. Aidan's work enabled the development of more targeted and environmentally friendly insecticides, earning him international recognition and accolades. His tireless efforts to unlock the secrets of the derris plant have had a lasting impact on the world of entomology and beyond.",
